/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STATUS-2026-09-10.md:31:## What is known about each route
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STATUS-2026-09-10.md:32:**First route — the bottleneck.** Held-out `R² 0.151`, pairwise ordering `0.650`; 79.3 % of target variance sits in whole-network coupled terms and 98.9 % of the externality is within-anchor so none cancels in ranking. An oracle removing only the cross-user externality reaches `0.902`. Verdict `TARGET_REFORMULATE`. Ridge reaches EV `+0.089`, positive on 10/10 leave-one-step-out folds; collision-bound variance is **zero**. The one admissible feature found bought exactly nothing because it is constant at all thirty anchors. A test of the cheapest remaining repair — giving it the resource context the interaction head already consumes — is running.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STATUS-2026-09-10.md:34:**Second route — best posed.** Target verdict `TARGET_WELL_POSED`; its reviewer explicitly declined to redesign it. Ridge EV `+0.301`, positive on 8/8 folds. **But its stored survival flags are wrong on 822 of 1,784 rows** through an adapter that writes geometric legality into both the validity and survival fields. That repair is owed and has not been made.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STATUS-2026-09-10.md:36:**Third route — its named threat is refuted.** Learned interaction head 3.618 mean selection regret against a size-only prior's 13.114 and zero's 13.683: knowing the coalition size is worth 0.569, the learned head is worth 9.496. Its decision-level justification is the exact-pair replay: pairwise truncation reverses the winner at 27.8 % of anchors, 92 % of those beyond the project's margin.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STATUS-2026-09-10.md:40:2. repair the second route's adapter defect;
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STATUS-2026-09-10.md:46:Roughly 3 to 3.5 in 10, with the first route as the binding constraint. Composition matters more than the number: the third route improved today, the second is best-posed but needs its adapter fixed, and the first has no known path until the running test reports.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-TERMINOLOGY-2026-09-10.md:1:# Controller note — what to call the thing the third route predicts, and why "coordination" was the wrong word
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-TERMINOLOGY-2026-09-10.md:5:The three routes are **not three parallel, same-shaped things**:
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-TERMINOLOGY-2026-09-10.md:10:**If users were independent, Ψ would be identically zero and the third route would have nothing to predict.** So the interaction is not an extra component bolted on — it is that route's entire job description.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-TERMINOLOGY-2026-09-10.md:13:1. the third route itself, which predicts the interaction residual;
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-TERMINOLOGY-2026-09-10.md:20:**The estimand — what the third route predicts.** *Interaction term* is the general-purpose name and fits our eight arms exactly, since they are the complete 2³ factorial. In cooperative game theory the same object is the **Harsanyi dividend**, the Möbius transform coefficient, and for coalitions of size three or more our Ψ is the sum of all Möbius coefficients above first order. Information theory calls the positive case **synergy**. Economics and networking call the cross-user part an **externality** — which our own target-design review already used, as *cross-user externality*.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-TERMINOLOGY-2026-09-10.md:33:| the quantity the third route predicts | **interaction term**, noting it generalises the Harsanyi dividend |
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ERRATA-2026-09-10.md:21:**8. "The first head has no predictive value; held-out explained variance is negative."** That was a k-nearest-neighbour failure concentrated on one held-out step. Ridge reaches **+0.089** on the same split and beats the constant predictor on **10 of 10** leave-one-step-out folds, with a median of +0.180. The route has **zero** collision-bound variance. *Corrected by two independent estimator audits.*
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-PAIR-INSUFFICIENCY-2026-09-10.md:29:Together with the architecture comparison — where a resource-aware and a ranker variant both beat pairwise on mean regret, 5.25 and 5.68 against 7.00 — this converts the third-order head from "a quantity we can measure" into "a quantity the decision needs". It is the strongest support the C3 route has had. It remains development evidence.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1-INTERFACE-2026-09-10.md:1:# Controller finding — the first route's problem is its interface, not its features
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1-INTERFACE-2026-09-10.md:5:I assembled it from three of today's reports: the design review measured the first route's pairwise ordering at 0.650 against 0.902 for an oracle that removes only the cross-user externality; the sufficiency diagnostic found the interaction head already receives 163 resource-context coordinates the per-user head does not; and the parametrisation comparison measured those coordinates as worth 1.067 in mean selection regret. So: perhaps the missing information already exists, is already consumed at decision time, and the per-user head simply does not receive it.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1-INTERFACE-2026-09-10.md:10:The coordinate formulas are admissible: they are built from the reference assignment and the decision-time tape, read static cross-gain arrays, and accept no evaluator or outcome. But **a coalition-wide vector depends on the other proposed members' actions, while the first route's interface is action-local.** The stored values could therefore not be handed over; the same 163 formulas had to be rebuilt from the reference profile and the focal user-action alone.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1-INTERFACE-2026-09-10.md:14:**The useful variation in those coordinates is coalition-level, and the first route is per-user by interface. It cannot receive it.** This is not a feature-plumbing problem.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1-INTERFACE-2026-09-10.md:27:It closes the cheapest remaining repair for the identified bottleneck, and it is the **second** first-route repair today to buy exactly nothing — the first being an admissible feature that turned out constant at all thirty anchors. The difference is that this time the reason is structural: any real fix would have to change what that route sees at the interface, which is fixed by contract §C1 — the same class of change I declined earlier today for the third route on the grounds that it removes the structure the owner's requirement is stated over.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1-INTERFACE-2026-09-10.md:29:**It does not establish that the first route's ablation marginal is zero.** These diagnostics measure how well its target can be predicted from pre-decision information. The owner's contrast measures whether informative source training changes the committed outcome relative to neutral training — a different question. The tier probe measured that dropping this route changes **12 to 26 proposed assignments** at every anchor tested, so it demonstrably moves the decision. Whether it moves it for the better is exactly what has never been run.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1-INTERFACE-2026-09-10.md:32:I am proposing no third repair. Two of my own have now bought nothing. The next step is to run the contrast and let the route answer for itself.
