/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:6:## Why the three routes are not interchangeable in the deployed system
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:7:Read from the live implementation, which is the three-route model and profile selector, not the older compatibility path:
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:9:- **the first route's** per-action outputs enter every candidate's score **and** the per-user argmax that builds the reference proposal and repairs an infeasible one;
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:10:- **the second route's** outputs do the same, independently;
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:11:- **the third route** supplies a single whole-set scalar to ranking only, is **hard zero on empty and singleton sets**, and never touches the proposal or repair path.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:13:A single set-conditioned score collapses the ranking path into one head. The leave-one-out arms for the first and third routes then no longer mean what the contract says they mean.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:16:A shared direct readout consuming the original heads' outputs — the first route entering through its per-user terms, the third through its interaction scalar, the second through its own sum — would keep three source interventions defined. Three things disqualify it now:
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:20:3. **The all-neutral control stops being all-neutral.** It would be neutral for the three original routes while still containing informative training in the shared readout, so the claim sentence becomes conditional on that predictor rather than describing a three-head system with all learned supervision neutral.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:22:The alternative of retargeting the third route's supervision was also examined and rejected: it supplies unilateral supervision even to the neutral arm, which changes the sealed labels, the neutral training and the control background. It is not the contracted contrast.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:24:Under the fixed requirements neither construction conforms: §B4 fixes the factor identity, §C1 fixes the per-user surrogates, §C2 fixes residual-only third-route supervision, singleton zero anchoring and the deployed sum. Retaining the exact decomposition as a reporting known-answer test would not make a different deployed score satisfy §C2.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DIRECT-2026-09-10.md:30:The ranking result stands as a measurement: direct prediction ranks better on these pools. If the project ever pursues a selector whose contribution claim is about decision quality rather than three separable routes, that measurement is the starting point. It is simply not usable for the requirement as the owner has stated it.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **FORMAL-LEARNER** — heads identical to the V0.23 heterogeneous Catfish trainer's configuration (architecture, optimiser and settings, batch construction, epoch budget and stopping rule), with input dimensions changed to the sealed schemas; the literal configuration values are copied from the legacy trainer's frozen config into spec v1 at seal time (no re-tuning). The set head uses the same optimiser settings.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-PARAMETRISATION-2026-09-10.md:16:**The extrapolation problem was solved by data, not by reformulation.** Exact labels at size 100 were generated and included — 180 training, 60 validation, 60 test rows — and out-of-support selections then fall to **0.00 % for both arms**. That is precisely the third of the three routes the external round identified, and neither parametrisation deserves credit for it. Sizes 7 to 99 remain absent, so the size curve is observed at 2–6 and 100, not continuously.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FEASIBILITY-2026-09-10.md:47:| contract v1.1 amendment, 2026-09-09 | measured **three**-contrast conjunction power `0.675` at `delta* = +2%`, 16 seeds, 160 dates |
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-NOVELTY-CLOSED-2026-09-10.md:31:**It closes the mechanism paper.** Two independent strategic reviews recommended making the physical mechanism the contribution and treating the learned coordinator as a follow-on. That route is now shut on novelty grounds, and the owner's decision on that reframing no longer needs taking.
